From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonardo Bornia <leonardo.bornia@toradex.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:24:43 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] L4TLauncher: only use the Torizon boot mode with Secure Boot

L4TLauncher takes its boot mode from the L4TDefaultBootMode variable
and from "bootmode=" in its load options. Both can be written from the
running system, and the modes other than the Torizon one boot the
kernel partition or the recovery partition: Android boot images that
only need a signature that verifies against db. The image that
initrd-flash boots is one, and it gives access to the storage of the
device over USB.

With UEFI Secure Boot enabled, use the Torizon boot mode whatever the
variable and the load options say, so that the only thing booted is a
signed UKI with a root filesystem that the initramfs verifies.

The boot over USB in recovery mode (RCM) does not go through the boot
mode and is not changed.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Torizon specific]
Signed-off-by: Leonardo Bornia <leonardo.bornia@toradex.com>
---
 .../Application/L4TLauncher/L4TLauncher.c     | 23 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Silicon/NVIDIA/Application/L4TLauncher/L4TLauncher.c b/Silicon/NVIDIA/Application/L4TLauncher/L4TLauncher.c
index b204617..4f92d19 100644
--- a/Silicon/NVIDIA/Application/L4TLauncher/L4TLauncher.c
+++ b/Silicon/NVIDIA/Application/L4TLauncher/L4TLauncher.c
@@ -2127,6 +2127,29 @@ ProcessBootParams (
     }
   }
 
+  //
+  // Torizon: with UEFI Secure Boot enabled, only the Torizon boot mode boots
+  // a system that is verified. The other modes boot the kernel or the
+  // recovery partition, and both the L4TDefaultBootMode variable and the
+  // load options that select them can be written from the running system.
+  //
+  if (IsSecureBootEnabled () && (BootParams->BootMode != NVIDIA_L4T_BOOTMODE_TORIZON)) {
+    ErrorPrint (L"%a: Secure Boot is enabled, using the Torizon boot mode\r\n", __FUNCTION__);
+    BootParams->BootMode = NVIDIA_L4T_BOOTMODE_TORIZON;
+    DataSize             = sizeof (BootParams->TorizonBootFlags);
+    Status               = gRT->GetVariable (
+                                  TORIZON_BOOTFLAGS_VARIABLE_NAME,
+                                  &gNVIDIAPublicVariableGuid,
+                                  NULL,
+                                  &DataSize,
+                                  &BootParams->TorizonBootFlags
+                                  );
+    if (EFI_ERROR (Status)) {
+      ErrorPrint (L"Failed to read boot flags (err %r)\r\n", Status);
+      BootParams->TorizonBootFlags = 0;
+    }
+  }
+
   // Find valid Rootfs Chain. If not, select recovery kernel
   Status = ValidateRootfsStatus (BootParams);
   if (EFI_ERROR (Status)) {
